<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: National Irish H1 pretax profit up 1.2 pct.</title>
<headline>National Irish H1 pretax profit up 1.2 pct.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to March 31, 1997</p>
<p>			  (million punts unless stated)</p>
<p> Net interest income    23.81		 vs 22.99</p>
<p> Total operating income 33.09		 vs 31.39</p>
<p> Bad debt provision     0.75		  vs 0.17</p>
<p> Pretax profit	    11.11		 vs 10.98</p>
<p> Taxation		   4.48		  vs 3.89</p>
<p> Total assets	     1,428		 vs 1,158</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of the Irish banking group is National Irish Bank, a unit of the National Australia Bank Group. The pretax profit figure is after provisions for bad and doubtful debts.</p>
<p>-- Dublin newsroom + 353 1 676 9775</p>
</text>
